<p class="lead">
  The MCP connector gives an assistant (Claude Desktop, Claude Code…) access to this site's
  database: it can check the advertised specs of a box, look up the limits of a SoC and the
  revisions of a model, with the status and sources of every value. It is read-only and contacts no
  server by default.
</p>

<h2>What it can do</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th scope="col">Tool</th>
      <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">
        <code>check_box</code>
      </th>
      <td>
        Compares the advertised model, SoC, RAM, storage, Ethernet and video with the known limits.
        Returns an overall verdict and one verdict per criterion, with status, basis and sources.
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">
        <code>get_soc</code>
      </th>
      <td>Limits of a SoC, community findings, listed boxes.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">
        <code>get_model</code>
      </th>
      <td>
        Revisions of a model (official or merely reported SoCs), level of confirmation, reported
        cases.
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">
        <code>search</code>
      </th>
      <td>Finds a SoC, a model or a case by name, alias, brand or keyword.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>
  Every tool accepts a <code>language</code> parameter (<code>fr</code> or <code>en</code>).
</p>
<p class="notice">
  Like the site, the connector never proves that a box is genuine: "plausible" only means that no
  impossibility was detected.
</p>

<h2>Installation</h2>
<p>
  The connector is not published on npm yet: build it from the repository (Node 20 or later and
  pnpm).
</p>
<pre><code>git clone https://github.com/Nicolasmar91/tvbox-check.git
cd tvbox-check
pnpm install
pnpm build:mcp</code></pre>
<p>
  The program is then at <code>packages/mcp/dist/index.js</code>.
</p>

<h3>Claude Desktop</h3>
<p>
  In the <code>claude_desktop_config.json</code> file (Settings, Developer, Edit config):
</p>
<pre><code>{`{
  "mcpServers": {
    "tvbox-check": {
      "command": "node",
      "args": ["/path/to/tvbox-check/packages/mcp/dist/index.js"],
      "env": { "TVBOX_CHECK_LANG": "en" }
    }
  }
}`}</code></pre>

<h3>Claude Code</h3>
<pre><code>claude mcp add tvbox-check -e TVBOX_CHECK_LANG=en -- node /path/to/tvbox-check/packages/mcp/dist/index.js</code></pre>

<h2>Settings</h2>
<ul>
  <li>
    <code>TVBOX_CHECK_LANG</code>: default language of the answers, <code>fr</code> or
    <code>en</code> (default: <code>en</code>).
  </li>
  <li>
    <code>TVBOX_CHECK_DB_URL</code>: optional. HTTPS address of an up-to-date database, for example
    <code>https://tvbox-check.nm-labs.dev/data/db.json</code>. It is validated against the schema
    before use; on failure the bundled database is kept. Without this variable, nothing goes over
    the network.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Security</h2>
<ul>
  <li>The four tools are read-only: they change nothing and run no command.</li>
  <li>
    Summaries and source titles come from public third-party pages: they are returned as data, which
    the assistant must never treat as instructions.
  </li>
  <li>
    The published database is freely reusable (CC BY 4.0) at
    <a href="/data/db.json">
      <code>/data/db.json</code>
    </a>
    .
  </li>
</ul>
